# J.A.R.V.I.S. project rules

## Scope
- Work only inside this project unless the user explicitly requests a specific external path.
- Preserve the existing Python, FastAPI, frontend, and Windows automation architecture.
- Keep credentials, API keys, cookies, and tokens in `.env`; never print or commit them.

## Verification
- Never claim that an app, page, file, or action succeeded without a tool response or visible UI/CDP/UI-Automation verification.
- Report the actual error when an action cannot be verified.
- For multi-step commands, execute and verify each step in order and stop at the first failed step.
- Prefer existing connected TradingView/Edge sessions over opening duplicate browser windows.

## Desktop actions
- Use the existing bounded desktop executor, UI Automation, and TradingView controller.
- Do not enable unrestricted shell execution, arbitrary downloads, registry changes, broad process termination, or hidden persistence.
- Installing a dependency requires a named package, a clear project need, and a verification step.
- Keep screenshots/OCR explicit and user-requested; use accessibility/UI context as the default observation path.

## Financial and external actions
- Market research and Paper Trading preparation are allowed.
- Never submit real-money trades, send messages/emails, delete data, shut down/restart the system, or change account settings without explicit confirmation immediately before the irreversible action.
- Treat financial information as scenarios and analysis, not investment advice.

## Code quality
- Make surgical changes, reuse existing helpers, and run the smallest relevant syntax check or test.
- Do not add fake/demo success values or silently swallow errors.
- Keep the safe-mode behavior and audit logging intact.
